{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def terminators' -A3 src/cljc/yin/vm/code.cljc; sed -n '258,272p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '775,806p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"26:(def terminators\n27-  \"Instructions after which control never reaches pc + 1.\"\n28-  #{:jump :return :halt})\n29-\n(defn active-continuation?\n  \"Returns true when the currently active continuation should keep stepping.\"\n  [vm]\n  (and (not (:blocked? vm)) (not (:halted? vm))))\n\n\n(defn ready-for-ingress?\n  \"Returns true when the VM is between evaluations and can accept another\n   program batch: not blocked, nothing scheduled or waiting, no active\n   continuation, and no loaded work.\n\n   This predicate gates observer coordination above the VM. The VM itself\n   never polls a program stream: `step` and `run` execute loaded work only.\"\n  [vm]\n  (let [has-bytecode? (contains? vm :bytecode)\n\n\n(deftest closure-in-blocked-environment-survives-fenced-recovery-test\n  (let [source (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                                 (let1 'f (lam [] (lit 42))\n                                       (let1 'input (make-stream-ast)\n                                             (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 'input)))\n                                                   (app (v 'f)))))))\n        source-closure (get-in source [:wait-set 0 :env 'f])\n        {:keys [machine record]} (export/enter source)\n        {:keys [serve!]} (served-table)\n        prepared (export/prepare machine record serve! nil)\n        frozen (export/freeze machine (:record prepared))\n        calls (atom 0)\n        restored (export/rehydrate-fenced\n                   (new-machine {:origin :fresh :capability-secret \"fresh-secret\"}) (:bytes frozen)\n                   {:address (:address frozen)\n                    :attach (fn [_descriptor]\n                              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n                               :dao.stream/handle (counting-handle calls)})})\n        closure (get-in restored [:record :wait-set 0 :env 'f])]\n    (is (values/closure? source-closure) (pr-str (:wait-set source)))\n    (is (= :ok (:status restored)) (pr-str restored))\n    (is (values/closure? closure))\n    (is (values/owned-by? closure (:owner (:machine restored))))\n    (is (not (values/owned-by? closure (:owner source))))\n    (is (zero? @calls))\n    (is (= :exporting (vm/gate-mode (:machine restored))))\n    (is (empty? (:wait-set (:machine restored))))\n    (is (= (vec (:body-bytes frozen))\n           (vec (:bytes (export/encode (:machine restored) (:record restored))))))))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md'\ns=open(p).read().replace('format \"'`:yin.code/semantic`'\"','format \"'`:yin.semantic/code`'\"')\ns=s.replace('A parked-phase child must be blocked; a running\\\\nchild may be blocked or halted as the engine\\\\'s install transition\\\\nallows. Explicitly parked children that cannot finish the install are\\\\nnot silently relabeled. Apply the existing complete-install restrictions\\\\nof UCF 7.4.3.', 'Phase and child kind are independent: each of the two phases admits\\\\neach of blocked, parked and halted, provided the child independently\\\\npasses the full quiescence and body checks. Preserve both fields; do not\\\\nintroduce a stricter phase/kind pairing. This is the landed UCF 7.4.3\\\\nrule, including an explicitly parked child.')\ns=s.replace('For stack, resume PC may equal the final instruction count only where\\\\nthe landed b2 transition would legally return/halt there; reconstruction\\\\nuses row-at\\\\'s one-past rule, never an out-of-range instruction fetch.\\\\nRegister\\\\'s inclusive body ranges and validator govern its PC endpoints.\\\\nSemantic retains its existing strict PC bound.', 'For stack, the saved resume PC and every return PC are strictly inside\\\\nthe captured code-space length. An admitted b2 image ends at a jump,\\\\nreturn or halt, not a suspending instruction; no valid park needs an\\\\nout-of-range resume fetch. The general row-at one-past rule does not\\\\nwaive this eligibility check. Register\\\\'s inclusive body ranges and\\\\nvalidator govern its PC endpoints. Semantic retains its existing strict\\\\nPC bound.')\ns=s.replace('Include empty base, current-row boundary PC and code hash corruption.', 'Include empty base, row-boundary validation and code hash corruption.')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
